# nr-office-author-brief: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own).
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change: the crate is pure and has no caller yet.)

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml
[workspace] members: add, right after `"crates/mixdog-office-quality",`:

    "crates/mixdog-office-author",

[workspace.dependencies]: add, right after the `mixdog-office-quality = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-quality" }` line:

    mixdog-office-author = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-author" }

## 2. native/core/Cargo.lock
Lead regenerates it offline (`cargo update --workspace --offline`). The new package `mixdog-office-author` has the
dependencies `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-office-base`, `mixdog-office-design`, `mixdog-office-quality`,
`mixdog-workspace-hack` and `serde_json` (all already in the lock; no new external crate and no new feature of one).
Its dev-dependency is `mixdog-office-base` with the feature `test-support`, which the base crate already declares.

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing: the new crate's Cargo.toml carries the `mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }`
dependency as every office crate does. If the hakari rule of the workspace wants more features unified, regenerate.

